5. TPM & BitLocker

TPM — Trusted Platform Module

TPM is a hardware-based security component used to securely store and process cryptographic information.

It can help with:

- Device security
- Key protection
- BitLocker
- Secure boot-related security features

---

TPM + Removable Drive

On supported systems, BitLocker can use a removable USB drive containing a startup key.

This can be used as part of the process of unlocking a protected Windows drive.

TPM
 +
USB startup key
 =
Additional BitLocker authentication option

THM may refer to TPM 1.2 or later in the context of this feature.

---

VSS — Volume Shadow Copy Service

VSS stands for:

Volume Shadow Copy Service

It is a Windows service that allows Windows and applications to create consistent snapshots/copies of files or volumes.

It is used by features such as:

- Backup systems
- System Restore
- Other applications requiring consistent snapshots

