9. Reading Files

"type"

Displays the contents of a text file.

type file.txt

Best suited for shorter text files.

---

"more"

Displays text page-by-page, making it easier to read long files.

more file.txt

---

10. File Management Commands

"copy"

Copies a file from one location to another.

copy source.txt destination.txt

---

"move"

Moves a file or directory.

move source.txt destination

---

"del" / "erase"

Deletes files.

del file.txt

or:

erase file.txt

«Be careful with delete commands because deleted files may not be easily recoverable.»

---

11. Process Management

"tasklist"

Displays currently running processes.

tasklist

---

Filtering with "/fi"

"/fi" means filter.

Example:

tasklist /fi "imagename eq sshd.exe"

This filters the results to show processes whose image name is:

sshd.exe

---

"eq"

"eq" means:

Equal to

So:

imagename eq sshd.exe

means:

Image name = sshd.exe

---

12. Terminating a Process

"taskkill"

Used to terminate a running process.

Using PID:

taskkill /pid TARGET_PID

Example:

taskkill /pid 1234

Where:

1234 → Target Process ID (PID)

You can first find the PID using:

tasklist

and then use:

taskkill /pid 1234

«Terminating system-critical processes can cause applications or Windows to become unstable.»

